 - 2026-08-24: Gemma-4-26B-A4B one-family flagship source shard (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete_gemma4_26b_a4b_runtime_and_immutable_source_shard_without_quality_claim; results/experiment_6583_gemma4_26b_a4b_flagship_source_shard.json
 - 2026-08-24: Operational retrospective for 2026.08.572: 5 experiments completed in the locked 16.5-minute window, including 3 compute-bound tasks. Qwen3.6 one-family flagship source shard formed the reported 15-minute critical path, but no data available this milestone identifies the slow phase. GPU 1 was active at 94% while GPU 0 was unused; the locked compute-idle field remains false because a single-model task correctly uses one GPU. No data available this milestone establishes a parallel load of 2 or more models or a missed DualGPURunner engagement. Next-cycle tooling should benchmark 8-16-question batches, dispatch ready independent model jobs to the free device, and preserve task-linked phase, GPU, model-count, and runner receipts. Estimated savings: 0% because no measured counterfactual was supplied. Artifact: results/operational_retro_2026_08_572.json.
 - 2026-08-24 (outer loop): Induction diagnosis reports the cause it diagnosed (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6710). `induction_skipped` could not resolve the question it is read to answer. `execute_bounded_llm_reinduction` pre-set `skipped = "no_reachable_plan_after_refinement"` before any round ran, and two sites that diagnosed a real cause wrote it only to the per-round record: the held-out transition verification failure and the selection-or-planning exception. Four sibling sites already wrote both. So an attempt whose every round failed DYNAMICS verification was reported under a PLANNING label — 9 of 18 live skip records were that default. Both sites now set the outer variable. Two further gaps closed alongside: the proposer's per-channel character counters had no consumer in the refinement loop, so each round now records its own `channel_chars` by differencing two monotone reads; and the chat channel-split accumulation moved out of the request method into `LocalGGUFProposer._record_chat_channel_split`, so it is testable in one place. The harness digest's dependence on `heldout_accuracy` / `accepted_by_heldout_verifier` is now pinned by test. Tests: `tests/python/test_arc_induction_diagnosis_6710.py` (10 tests, SCENARIO-ARC-WMTE-6710-1..7), 7 mutations each RED then restored byte-identical. Two candidate changes were REVERTED as decorative when their mutations stayed green — both duplicated writes the round's `row.update(...)` block already made. REQ id note: the first draft used REQ-ARC-WMTE-6700, which collides with the committed induction-quality-scorer REQ; renumbered to 6710.
+- 2026-08-25: V573 terminal recovery and bounded execution contract (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: all six V572 terminal states and three Exp6584 hard-limit attempts replay; V573 model tasks are bounded; no science verdict was created; results/experiment_6585_v573_terminal_recovery_and_execution_contract.json
